      "summary": "Cardrona is open for skiing and snowboarding today, with a fresh refresh overnight topping up the recent storm snow. The new snow is sitting on a firm underlying snowpack, leaving conditions variable off trail. The mountain is currently -2°C with 8 km/h winds and 13 km/h gusts, with some mountain fog at the base and across parts of the mountain. Cloud should clear to finer conditions this morning, with a light northeasterly flow. Main Basin and Valley View lifts are scheduled to open from 8:30 am, with Captains, Willows, Soho and T-Bar following from 9:00 am. The latest official report lists Kindy Conveyor, Learner Conveyors, McDougall’s Chondola, Whitestar Express, Valley View, Captains Express, T-Bar, Soho Express and Willow’s Quad open, while Wells Pipe Platter is closed. Terrain including Learners Slopes, McDougall's, Whitestar, Captains, Soho, WIllows, Mt Cardrona, Arcadia Chutes and Summit is open. (Issued: 7 Sep, approximately 6:30 am) The access road is chain-free, but chains must be carried, with an active road-hazard advisory. JWI Rail Jam is scheduled in McPark from 11:00 am–1:30 pm, open to all ages on skis or snowboards. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 9 / 10 Runs Open 0 / 38 Percent open 0 %",
